            "title": "DataHawk Plugin for BASE3 Framework",
            "summary": "The DataHawk plugin extends the BASE3 framework with a schema-driven query engine for reporting and data access.",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "id": "section_1",
                    "template": "short_overview",
                    "title": "Introduction to DataHawk",
                    "body": "DataHawk is a plugin for the BASE3 framework that provides a schema-driven query engine. It allows for structured JSON queries that are compiled to SQL and executed through the BASE3 IDatabase abstraction.",
                    "interaction": {
                        "type": "reading",
                        "prompt": "Read through the introduction to understand the basic functionality of DataHawk."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "section_2",
                    "template": "micro_learning",
                    "title": "Key Features",
                    "body": "DataHawk supports various query types including SELECT, INSERT, DELETE, and TRANSACTION. It also features automatic join planning, sensitivity and data protection, and schema management.",
                    "interaction": {
                        "type": "reflection",
                        "prompt": "Reflect on how these features might enhance your data management tasks."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "section_3",
                    "template": "checklist",
                    "title": "Query Syntax",
                    "body": "DataHawk uses a structured JSON format for queries. Here are some examples of different query types:",
                    "interaction": {
                        "type": "question",
                        "prompt": "Which query type do you think you will use most frequently and why?"
                    },
                    "items": [
                        "SELECT: Used for retrieving data from the database.",
                        "INSERT: Used for adding new data into the database.",
                        "DELETE: Used for removing data from the database.",
                        "TRANSACTION: Used for executing multiple queries atomically."
                    ]
                }
            ],
